==============================================================================
Codex irreducibility tricks -> LRC14 proof-transfer atlas
==============================================================================

A. Irreducibility tricks as LRC proof carriers
  mod_p_convolution_blocker
    poly: Find a prime p for which f mod p has no nontrivial split.
    LRC : Find a denominator family, such as Q27, whose safe-twist obligations cannot all be covered.
    use : Turns local survivor emptiness into a global no-counterexample certificate in a normalized class.
    risk: Fails on ramified packets where residue data collapse.
  eisenstein_newton_valuation
    poly: Use p-adic heights/Newton slopes when f mod p looks reducible.
    LRC : Use prime-ideal carry data: many speeds in one ideal, one primitive escape, next-shell witness.
    use : Explains the two HYP-2470 exceptions as ramified local packets rather than random misses.
    risk: Needs a clean inequality replacing the scan over q=31,33.
  gauss_primitive_normal_form
    poly: Strip content; prove irreducibility for the primitive part.
    LRC : Normalize rows by gcd, core retention, carry window, and Bprime/opening channels.
    use : Prevents wasting effort on nonprimitive 7-multiple shadows.
    risk: Can hide large outside-window runners unless paired with a normalizer.
  hensel_recombination_ladder
    poly: Factor locally, then ask whether local factors recombine globally.
    LRC : Lift Q27 residue/fiber packets through divisor shells and missing plain-shell layers.
    use : Suggests storing survivor ledgers instead of only first-witness denominators.
    risk: May be too detailed unless the state space is compressed.
  cohn_perron_digit_dominance
    poly: Large-base digit/value dominance can certify irreducibility.
    LRC : Large speed as a carry digit: either it opens Bprime or folds to a lower carry address.
    use : A route for outside-window normalization after the eight-core carry-window theorem.
    risk: Dominance constants are the hard part.
  singh_factor_capture_budget
    poly: A value f(m) with small Omega limits possible irreducible factors.
    LRC : Treat blocker obligations as tokens to allocate among added speeds; small budget forces failure.
    use : Turns HYP-2465/HYP-2470 MILP certificates into proof-shaped resource inequalities.
    risk: The exact Singh theorem has hypotheses; the LRC use is an analogy until formalized.
  fixed_divisor_admissibility
    poly: Bunyakovsky admissibility forbids one prime from dividing every value.
    LRC : No single residue/clock should be allowed to cover all twists without a compensating opening.
    use : Pushes the 13-clock residual toward a finite exceptional atlas.
    risk: Admissibility is necessary, not sufficient.
  galois_cycle_type_sequence
    poly: Factorization mod p gives Frobenius cycle-type data.
    LRC : First-witness denominator sequence gives cover-type data: which shells open which packets.
    use : Could classify below-eight-core packets by cycle-type-like signatures.
    risk: Mostly descriptive until a Chebotarev-like replacement lemma is found.
  discriminant_ramification_map
    poly: Bad primes divide the discriminant and mark ramified local behavior.
    LRC : Sparse unresolved deletion addresses mark ramification: add shell 31/33/41 or Bprime.
    use : Treats finite exceptions as data to resolve, not as theorem failure.
    risk: Requires avoiding post-hoc overfitting.
  integral_convolution_lift_ilp
    poly: Reducibility is existence of an integer coefficient-grid lift.
    LRC : Q-blocking is existence of an obligation-cover lift by added speeds.
    use : Makes exact infeasibility certificates the analogue of irreducibility certificates.
    risk: MILP dual certificates must be extracted to become human proof.

